{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"Pbe68a503"},"owner_reference":"#2498","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"Pbe68a503\",\"feature\":\"backlog-core-decompose\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Decompose backlog_core/operations.py (5407 lines) and backlog_core/server.py (4640 lines) into three cohesive sibling modules (section_filter.py, view_assembly.py, view_budget.py) with zero consumer edits and zero behavioural change, except one deliberate, scoped fix: the _apply_body_section_filter dual-output contract becomes a pure function whose caller owns the result.body assignment.\",\"context\":\"## Source artifacts\\n\\n- Architecture spec: `artifact_read(item_id=2498, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")` \\u2014 exact signatures, exact import blocks, exact diff for the dual-output fix.\\n- Feature context: `artifact_read(item_id=2498, artifact_type=\\\"feature-context\\\")` \\u2014 risk register R1-R6, desired outcomes.\\n- Codebase conventions: `artifact_read(item_id=2498, artifact_type=\\\"codebase-analysis\\\")`.\\n\\n## THREE CORRECTIONS THAT OVERRIDE THE ARCHITECT SPEC TEXT\\n\\nThe spec was written before these were decided. Where the spec text conflicts, these win.\\n\\n### Correction 1 \\u2014 ADR path\\n\\nUse `plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/ADR-2498-1-backlog-core-is-a-package.md`.\\nDo NOT use `docs/adr/backlog-core-is-a-package.md` (spec \\u00a71). The spec's own \\u00a77 Concern 4 flagged that path as wrong; independently re-verified 2026-09-03: no `docs/adr/` directory exists anywhere in this repo, while `plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/ADR-{issue}-{n}-{slug}.md` is the live convention with 8 existing files (ADR-1770-1, ADR-3072-1, ADR-3075-1..4, ADR-3082-1, ADR-3113-1) inside the very plugin that owns `backlog_core`.\\n\\n### Correction 2 \\u2014 7 orphan helpers move with their callers (spec \\u00a77 Concern 2 recommendation, ACCEPTED)\\n\\nEach has exactly one call site, entirely inside functions that are already moving. Moving them alongside their sole caller is strictly more cohesive at zero behavioural risk, and it removes the bottom-of-file circular-import workaround the spec otherwise requires.\\n\\n| Helper | operations.py/server.py line | Destination |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `_resolve_section_indices` | operations.py:2086 | section_filter.py |\\n| `_int_field` | operations.py:2554 | section_filter.py |\\n| `_compact_entry_count` | operations.py:2571 | section_filter.py |\\n| `_entry_owning_headers` | operations.py:2396 | view_assembly.py |\\n| `_render_paged_entry_body` | operations.py:2442 | view_assembly.py |\\n| `_sections_from_body_or_yaml` | operations.py:2766 | view_assembly.py |\\n| `_sections_index_from_result` | server.py:1928 | view_budget.py |\\n\\nRevised per-phase totals: Phase 1 = 8 symbols, Phase 2 = 8 symbols, Phase 3 = 6 symbols + `_enc`.\\n\\n**Consequence \\u2014 the spec's bottom-of-file placement rule (\\u00a72, \\u00a76.4) is CANCELLED.** Once each callee moves with its caller, `operations.py` and `server.py` no longer import anything back from the new modules for these helpers, so no circular import exists and the re-export block goes at the normal import position. Do not implement the workaround.\\n\\n**Re-verify before implementing.** This item's own churn history shows figures drifting between grooming and execution. Grep for callers of each of the 7 helpers immediately before moving it. If any helper turns out to have a caller that is NOT moving, leave it in place and import it back instead (the spec \\u00a73.2/\\u00a74.2 pattern), and record the divergence.\\n\\n### Correction 3 \\u2014 `_token_count` docstring accuracy (spec \\u00a77 Concern 3)\\n\\n`_token_count` has 3 call sites in `server.py`, only one of which is view-scoped: `_view_payload_token_count` (server.py:221, view-scoped), a match-context sizing call (server.py:648, unrelated tool), and a `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` pagination check (server.py:1582, `backlog_list`). `view_budget.py`'s module docstring MUST describe `_token_count` as general token-counting infrastructure co-located with its primary consumer \\u2014 NOT as view-exclusive. An agent reading that docstring must not conclude a `_token_count` change is safely view-scoped.\\n\\n## VERIFIED FACTS (re-checked against working-tree HEAD on 2026-09-03 during decomposition)\\n\\n- Every line number in the architect spec \\u00a73.1, \\u00a74.1, \\u00a76.1 matches live source exactly.\\n- `_apply_body_section_filter` has exactly ONE real caller: `operations.py:2872` inside `_assemble_view_content`. The two `server.py` hits (lines 981, 2263) are docstring/comment mentions, not calls. The spec's 1-caller claim is confirmed.\\n- `_sections_from_body_or_yaml` has 2 call sites (operations.py:2905, 2926), BOTH inside `_assemble_view_content` \\u2014 still a single-caller-function helper, so Correction 2 holds for it.\\n- Baseline MCP tool count for the backlog server: **46 tools**.\\n- Import-contract smoke check passes today (see acceptance criterion `import-contract`).\\n\\n## RE-EXPORT CONTRACT \\u2014 WIDER THAN THE SPEC STATES\\n\\nThe spec's re-export block covers the primary targets. Under Correction 2 it must ALSO cover the moved orphan helpers, because tests import them by name from the old path:\\n\\n- `backlog_core/tests/test_entry_owning_headers.py` and `test_section_boundary_scanner.py` do `from backlog_core.operations import _entry_owning_headers`.\\n- `backlog_core/tests/test_blank_section_normalization.py` does `from backlog_core.operations import _resolve_section_indices, view_item`.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` does `from backlog_core.server import _sections_index_from_result` and patches `backlog_core.server._enc.encode`.\\n\\nRisk R1 (feature-context \\u00a77) is the highest-cost risk on this item. The importable-name set is a PINNED CONTRACT verified by an explicit command, not an assumed consequence of correct editing.\\n\\n## SCOPE BOUNDARIES\\n\\n- No behaviour change except the \\u00a75 dual-output fix.\\n- No new `pyproject.toml`; no new distribution boundary; no collapse to one file.\\n- Plain module names (`section_filter.py`), NOT underscore-prefixed \\u2014 `sam_schema` precedent, per spec \\u00a77 Concern 1.\\n- No `@mcp.tool()`-decorated function leaves `server.py`.\\n- `from __future__ import annotations` first import in every new module; full return-type annotations on every function.\\n- Do NOT decompose the other 13 oversized `backlog_core` modules \\u2014 out of scope (feature-context \\u00a75).\\n- The `dh_core` destination question (feature-context \\u00a78.1) is NOT reopened here: this item decomposes into `backlog_core` siblings. `dh_core.operations` stays a facade and must keep importing successfully.\\n\\n## PARALLELISM\\n\\nT2 (operations.py Phase 1) and T4 (server.py Phase 3) touch DIFFERENT files and run concurrently. T3 depends on T2 (same file, plus an import edge). T1 (ADR) is documentation-only and runs concurrently with everything. Per repo policy, dispatch concurrent file-writing tasks into separate worktrees.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"\",\"issue\":\"2498\",\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"T0\",\"title\":\"T0 baseline \\u2014 author the view-path characterisation harness and capture pre-refactor state\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"dh:task-worker\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"python-engineering:modernpython\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-09-03T04:01:24.774757+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Feature-context risk R2 states that a green test suite proves no DETECTED regression, not correctness, and explicitly names the pagination x section-filter x over-budget interaction as the combination whose coverage is unproven. Feature-context section 8.4 leaves open whether the standard T0 bookend suffices or whether the view path needs a purpose-built characterisation pass. It needs one, and this task builds it before capturing the baseline.\\n\\nThis item also bundles ONE deliberate behavioural change (the dual-output fix, architect spec section 5) into an otherwise non-functional refactor. The characterisation record is what makes it possible to confirm that NOTHING ELSE changed.\\n\\nThis task has two parts and they are ordered: author the harness first (Part A), then capture (Part B). Part B's `view-path-characterisation` check-command invokes the file Part A creates.\",\"objective\":\"Build a deterministic characterisation harness for the view path, then record the observable state of every structured acceptance criterion before any refactor edit, so the TN gate can prove behavioural equivalence rather than merely asserting a green suite.\",\"requirements\":\"## PART A \\u2014 author the characterisation harness\\n\\n1. Write `plugins/development-harness/tests/characterise_view_path.py`.\\n\\n2. It must exercise `backlog_core.operations.view_item` (and/or `_assemble_view_content` directly where `view_item` cannot reach a combination) against an in-memory or fixture-backed `BacklogItem`, covering at minimum this matrix:\\n   - section filter: none / numeric index / comma-separated indices / regex form / substring form / a deliberate MISS (no matching section)\\n   - pagination: no offset+limit / offset only / limit only / offset+limit / offset past end\\n   - budget: a payload comfortably under `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` and one deliberately over it (exercising `_build_over_budget_view` and `_build_compact_manifest`)\\n   - `include_content` True and False (the False path is what sets `sections_index`)\\n\\n3. For each combination it prints one compact JSON object (per AGENTS.md: `json.dumps(...)`, no `indent=`) capturing the observable result \\u2014 at minimum