position-happened` (the three modules do not exist yet) and `adr-recorded` (the ADR file does not exist yet). They are what prove at TN that the work actually landed.\",\"constraints\":\"- Part A is purely ADDITIVE. Do not modify any existing test, fixture, or source module.\\n- Part B is read-and-record only. Change no source file.\\n- Compact JSON only (AGENTS.md: agent-facing output, no `indent=`).\\n- No `rich` \\u2014 plain `print()`/`json.dumps` (AGENTS.md: Rich hardcodes 80 columns with no TTY).\\n- `from __future__ import annotations` first import; full type annotations.\\n- Do not shorten, summarise, or elide any captured output.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"`plugins/development-harness/tests/characterise_view_path.py`; T0 baseline artifact registered on item 2498.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"- `plugins/development-harness/tests/characterise_view_path.py` exists; `uv run python plugins/development-harness/tests/characterise_view_path.py` exits 0 and prints one JSON line per combination.\\n- Running the harness twice produces byte-identical stdout.\\n- Every axis value listed in requirement 2 appears in at least one printed combination id.\\n- The section-filter-MISS combination's record includes a `body` field.\\n- `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/ -q` still passes (the new file is additive and is not collected).\\n- `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/tests/characterise_view_path.py` passes.\\n- A T0 artifact is registered on item 2498 with one entry per criterion id: `import-contract`, `view-path-characterisation`, `backlog-core-tests`, `wider-test-suite`, `lint-and-typecheck`, `mcp-tool-count`, `decomposition-happened`, `adr-recorded`.\\n- The `view-path-characterisation` entry contains the harness's complete stdout, untruncated.\\n- The `mcp-tool-count` entry records 46.\\n- `decomposition-happened` and `adr-recorded` are recorded as failing.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run the harness twice into two files and `diff` them \\u2014 must be identical.\\n2. Read the printed combination ids and confirm every axis value from requirement 2 appears.\\n3. Confirm the MISS combination prints `section_filter_miss: true` AND a `body` value.\\n4. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/ -q --collect-only 2>&1 | grep -c characterise_view_path` \\u2014 must be 0.\\n5. `artifact_read(item_id=2498, ...)` the registered T0 artifact and confirm all 8 criterion ids are present.\\n6. Confirm the artifact's `view-path-characterisation` stdout has the same line count as a fresh local harness run.\",\"handoff\":\"Unblocks T1, T2, T4. Report the exact set of combination ids produced so T5 can confirm the same set at TN.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"medium\",\"is_bookend\":true,\"bookend_type\":\"t0-baseline\"},{\"id\":\"T1\",\"title\":\"Phase 0 \\u2014 record the package-vs-launcher decision as ADR-2498-1\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"dh:task-worker\",\"dependencies\":[\"T0\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[\"T2\",\"T3\",\"T4\"],\"priority\":2,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"python-engineering:modernpython\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-09-03T04:01:24.774812+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Feature-context section 2.2 records that prior attempts at this refactor stalled on a recurring 'is backlog_core a script or a package?' confusion, and that the resolution (it is a package; the PEP 723 entrypoint is a launcher, not evidence of script-ness) was established during PR #2496. Feature-context outcome #5 requires that decision be written down durably. This is a copy-to-durable-location task \\u2014 the content already exists on the backlog item.\\n\\nThis task touches no Python source and runs concurrently with T2, T3, and T4.\",\"objective\":\"Write the already-decided package-vs-launcher determination to a durable location so the next session inherits the constraint instead of re-litigating it.\",\"requirements\":\"1. Read the 'Decision to record as an ADR' section of item #2498: `backlog_view(selector='#2498', summary=False, section='Decision to record as an ADR')`.\\n\\n2. Write `plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/ADR-2498-1-backlog-core-is-a-package.md`.\\n\\n   PATH CORRECTION \\u2014 this overrides architect spec section 1, which shows `docs/adr/backlog-core-is-a-package.md`. That path is wrong: no `docs/adr/` directory exists anywhere in this repository. The spec's own section 7 Concern 4 flagged it, and it was independently re-verified during decomposition. `plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/` is the live convention with 8 existing files and it belongs to the very plugin that owns `backlog_core`.\\n\\n3. Read at least two existing ADRs in that directory (e.g. `ADR-3113-1-orchestrator-manager-worker-role-vocabulary.md`, `ADR-3072-1-budget-applies-only-at-navigation.md`) and match their exact frontmatter and section structure. Do NOT invent a structure from memory.\\n\\n4. Transcribe the decision content from the backlog item. Do not draft new argument \\u2014 this records a decision already made, with the evidence already gathered.\",\"constraints\":\"- Documentation only. Change no Python source.\\n- Do not add provenance narrative or citations about this refactor task into the ADR beyond what the backlog item section already contains (repo rule: rules and ADRs carry the decision, not the history of arriving at it).\",\"expected_outputs\":\"`plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/ADR-2498-1-backlog-core-is-a-package.md`\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"- `plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/ADR-2498-1-backlog-core-is-a-package.md` exists.\\n- Its frontmatter fields and heading structure match the two ADRs read in requirement 3 (same field names, same section names, same order).\\n- Every factual claim in the ADR is traceable to the backlog item's 'Decision to record as an ADR' section.\\n- `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/ADR-2498-1-backlog-core-is-a-package.md` passes (markdownlint).\\n- No file is created under a `docs/adr/` path.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. `ls plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/` \\u2014 confirm the new file sits alongside the existing 8.\\n2. Compare the first 20 lines of the new ADR against an existing one \\u2014 confirm structural agreement on frontmatter field names.\\n3. `test ! -d docs/adr` \\u2014 confirm no novel third convention was created.\\n4. Confirm the ADR is not in `.claude/rules/` (repo policy: `.claude/rules/` holds current-requirement-only agent instructions; durable architecture decisions go in `docs/`).\",\"handoff\":\"Satisfies the `adr-recorded` structured criterion. T5 verifies.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"low\"},{\"id\":\"T2\",\"title\":\"Phase 1 \\u2014 extract backlog_core/section_filter.py (8 symbols from operations.py)\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T0\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[\"T1\",\"T4\"],\"priority\":2,\"complexity\":\"high\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"python-engineering:modernpython\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-09-03T04:01:24.774839+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Read the architect spec first: `artifact_read(item_id=2498, artifact_type='architect')`, sections 3 and 5. It gives exact signatures and the exact diff for the contract fix.\\n\\nThis task carries the plan's single deliberate behavioural change (the dual-output fix) alongside a no-behaviour-change move. Keep them separable: feature-context risk R3 warns that bundling them means a failure in one gets misattributed to the other. Implement the move first (Steps 1-3), confirm the suite is green, THEN apply the contract fix as a distinct step (Step 4), so a test failure tells you which change caused it.\",\"objective\":\"Move the eight section-filtering functions out of operations.py into a new cohesive backlog_core/section_filter.py, apply the dual-output contract fix to _apply_body_section_filter, and keep every symbol importable from backlog_core.operations.\",\"requirements\":\"## Symbols to move to `backlog_core/section_filter.py`\\n\\nFive primary targets (architect spec section 3.1):\\n- `_build_sections_index_from_body` (operations.py:2024)\\n- `_filter_sections` (2170)\\n- `_build_sections_metadata` (2297)\\n- `_build_sections_compact` (2367)\\n- `_apply_body_section_filter` (2634)\\n\\nThree orphan helpers, added per Correction 2 (see plan context):\\n- `_resolve_section_indices` (2086)\\n- `_int_field` (2554)\\n- `_compact_entry_count` (2571)\\n\\n## Step 1 \\u2014 RE-VERIFY the orphan helpers before moving them\\n\\nFor each of `_resolve_section_indices`, `_int_field`, `_compact_entry_count`, grep the whole `plugins/development-harness/` tree for callers. Confirm every caller is either (a) one of the eight symbols moving in this task, or (b) a test importing it by name from `backlog_core.operations` (which the re-export handles). If any helper has a caller that stays in `operations.py`, DO NOT move it \\u2014 leave it in place, import it back instead, and record the divergence in your report. Figures on this item have drifted between grooming and execution before.\\n\\n## Step 2 \\u2014 Create the module\\n\\n`from __future__ import annotations` as the first import. Module docstring naming the single responsibility: resolving a section selector against a body or item and narrowing to the matched sections.\\n\\nImports (architect spec section 3.2, adjusted for Correction 2 \\u2014 the three moved helpers are no longer imported back):\\n```python\\nfrom .models import BacklogItem, GroomedData, GroomedSectionMetadata, Section, SectionEntryMetadata, ViewItemResult\\nfrom .parsing import split_body_sections\\nfrom .operations import _merge_section_entries, _section_display_title, _slice_body_by_header_indices\\n```\\nCopy the exact `.models` names from `operations.py`'s existing import lines \\u2014 do not re-derive which types are needed.\\n\\nThe three names still imported back (`_merge_section_entries` 1995, `_section_display_title` 2007, `_slice_body_by_header_indices` 2605) are GENUINELY shared: each has a caller that is not moving (`_merge_section_entries` is also called by `_build_sections_from_yaml_item`, which moves in T3 to a DIFFERENT module; `_section_display_title` is also called by `_render_section_index`, which stays; `_slice_body_by_header_indices` is also called by `narrow_body_to_named_sections`, which stays). Verify each of those three claims with a grep before relying on it.\\n\\nCopy signatures and docstrings verbatim. `_filter_sections`, `_build_sections_metadata`, and `_build_sections_compact` are pure \\u2014 no contract change.\\n\\n## Step 3 \\u2014 Re-export from operations.py\\n\\nAdd `from .section_filter import (...)` to `operations.py` listing ALL EIGHT moved names. Normal import position (top of file) \\u2014 the bottom-of-file placement workaround in architect spec section 2 is CANCELLED by Correction 2 and must not be implemented. Confirm no circular import by running the `import-contract` check command.\\n\\nThe re-export must cover the orphan helpers, not just the five primary targets: `backlog_core/tests/test_blank_section_normalization.py` does `from backlog_core.operations import _resolve_section_indices, view_item`.\\n\\nRun the full suite here, BEFORE Step 4. It must be green with zero test edits. If it is not, the move is wrong \\u2014 fix it before touching the contract.\\n\\n## Step 4 \\u2014 The dual-output contract fix (architect spec section 5)\\n\\n4a. Re-grep `_apply_body_section_filter(` across `plugins/development-harness/` and confirm the caller count. Verified during decomposition: exactly ONE real caller at `operations.py:2872` inside `_assemble_view_content`; the two `server.py` hits (lines 981, 2263) are docstring/comment mentions only. Confirm this is still true.\\n\\n4b. In `_apply_body_section_filter` (now in `section_filter.py`): delete the `result.body = body` line immediately before `return body`. KEEP the `result.section_filter_miss` and `result.section_filter_valid_names` assignments on the miss branch \\u2014 those are genuinely result-scoped signals with no return-value duplicate and are NOT part of the defect.\\n\\n4c. Update the docstring: drop the 'and result.body' clause from the summary line and from the Returns section, since the function no longer mutates `result.body`.\\n\\n4d. At the call site in `_assemble_view_content` (operations.py:2872 pre-move), add the caller-owned assignment:\\n```python\\n                body = _apply_body_section_filter(result, body, section)\\n                result.body = body          # caller now owns the assignment\\n                if result.section_filter_miss:\\n```\\nNote `_assemble_view_content` moves to `view_assembly.py` in T3 \\u2014 make the edit here; T3 carries it across.\\n\\n## Step 5 \\u2014 Test impact (architect spec section 5.3)\\n\\nFive test files import `_apply_body_section_filter` directly and call it standalone: `test_apply_body_section_filter_forms.py`, `test_section_filter_miss.py`, `test_view_section_form_resolution.py`, `test_view_sections_metadata_sync.py`, `test_section_boundary_scanner_live_3152.py`.\\n\\nRead each one's assertions. Any assertion reading `result.body` immediately after calling `_apply_body_section_filter` without reading the return value will now see the PRE-call value. Classify each such assertion explicitly:\\n- (a) already asserts on the return value \\u2192 no change, note it;\\n- (b) asserted the old dual-write \\u2192 that test was asserting the bug