n place and always sets `sections_index` when `include_content` is False.\\n\\n## Step 3 \\u2014 Carry the T2 call-site edit\\n\\n`_assemble_view_content` is where T2 added `result.body = body` after the `_apply_body_section_filter` call (architect spec section 5.2). That line moves with the function. Confirm it is present and correct in the new module after the move \\u2014 losing it silently reverts the dual-output fix and would show up at TN as a characterisation diff.\\n\\n## Step 4 \\u2014 Re-export from operations.py\\n\\nAdd `from .view_assembly import (...)` to `operations.py` listing ALL EIGHT moved names. Normal import position \\u2014 the bottom-of-file workaround is CANCELLED (Correction 2). The re-export must cover the orphan helpers: `backlog_core/tests/test_entry_owning_headers.py` and `test_section_boundary_scanner.py` do `from backlog_core.operations import _entry_owning_headers`.\",\"constraints\":\"- ZERO behavioural change in this phase. No test may be modified.\\n- Plain module name `view_assembly.py`.\\n- `from __future__ import annotations` first import; full return-type annotations.\\n- Do NOT implement the bottom-of-file re-export placement workaround.\\n- Do NOT move `_merge_section_entries` or `_render_section_index`.\\n- Do NOT touch `server.py`.\\n- Locate functions by name, not by the pre-T2 line numbers.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/view_assembly.py`; modified `operations.py`.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/view_assembly.py` exists containing the eight symbols (or fewer, with a recorded divergence per Step 1).\\n- The `import-contract` check command exits 0.\\n- `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/ -q` passes with ZERO test files modified by this task.\\n- `uv run pytest -q` passes.\\n- `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/*.py` passes.\\n- `operations.py` line count is lower than after T2.\\n- `_assemble_view_content`'s signature has no `paginate` parameter.\\n- The `result.body = body` line from T2 is present at the `_apply_body_section_filter` call site in the new module.\\n- No `@mcp.tool()`-decorated function moved. Module name is `view_assembly.py`, not `_view_assembly.py`.\\n- `server.py` is untouched.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run the `import-contract` check command \\u2014 must exit 0.\\n2. `uv run python plugins/development-harness/tests/characterise_view_path.py` and diff against the post-T2 record. It must be BYTE-IDENTICAL \\u2014 this phase changes no behaviour, so any difference at all is a regression. Stop and report rather than proceeding.\\n3. `git status --porcelain` \\u2014 confirm no file under any `tests/` directory is modified by this task. If one is, that is a regression signal, not a routine update: report it instead of committing it.\\n4. `grep -n 'def _assemble_view_content' -A 12 plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/view_assembly.py` \\u2014 confirm no `paginate` parameter.\\n5. Confirm the one-directional edge: grep `section_filter.py` for calls to any of this module's eight symbols \\u2014 expect zero.\\n6. `grep -n 'result.body = body' plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/view_assembly.py` \\u2014 confirm the T2 edit survived the move.\\n7. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/ -q` and `uv run pytest -q`.\",\"handoff\":\"Report the importable-name list `view_assembly.py` exposes and the post-T3 line count of `operations.py`. T5 verifies.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"high\"},{\"id\":\"T4\",\"title\":\"Phase 3 \\u2014 extract backlog_core/view_budget.py (6 symbols + _enc from server.py)\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T0\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[\"T1\",\"T2\",\"T3\"],\"priority\":2,\"complexity\":\"high\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engin