.py:1928)\\n\\nCorrection 2 CHANGES the spec here: spec section 6.4 says `_sections_index_from_result` stays in `server.py` and is imported BACK by `view_budget.py`, which forces bottom-of-file placement. It now MOVES to `view_budget.py` alongside its two sole callers (`_build_compact_manifest`, `_build_over_budget_view`), so there is no back-import and NO bottom-of-file workaround.\\n\\n## Step 1 \\u2014 RE-VERIFY `_sections_index_from_result`\\n\\nGrep `plugins/development-harness/` for callers. Verified during decomposition: its only non-test references are `_build_compact_manifest` and `_build_over_budget_view`, both moving. `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` does `from backlog_core.server import _sections_index_from_result` \\u2014 handled by the re-export. If a non-moving caller exists in `server.py`, leave it in place and import it back instead (spec section 6.4 pattern), place `server.py`'s re-export block below its definition, and record the divergence.\\n\\n## Step 2 \\u2014 Create the module\\n\\n```python\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom typing import Final\\n\\nimport tiktoken\\n\\nfrom . import models as _models\\n```\\nNo `from .server import ...` line \\u2014 Correction 2 removes the need for it.\\n\\nMODULE DOCSTRING \\u2014 Correction 3 applies and is not optional. `_token_count` has three call sites in `server.py` and only ONE is view-scoped: `_view_payload_token_count` (server.py:221, view-scoped, stays in server.py), a match-context sizing call (server.py:648, an unrelated tool), and a `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` pagination check (server.py:1582, `backlog_list` \\u2014 a different tool with a different budget constant). The docstring MUST describe `_token_count` as general token-counting infrastructure co-located with its primary consumer, NOT as view-exclusive, and MUST name the two non-view consumers. An agent reading this docstring later must not conclude that a `_token_count` change is safely view-scoped.\\n\\n## Step 3 \\u2014 server.py import block (architect spec section 6.3 \\u2014 do not skip)\\n\\nReplace the original definitions in place with:\\n```python\\nfrom .view_budget import (\\n    _VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET,\\n    _build_compact_manifest,\\n    _build_over_budget_view,\\n    _enc,\\n    _filter_view_sections,\\n    _sections_index_from_result,\\n    _token_count,\\n)\\n```\\nThis MUST be a plain module-level import, NOT conditional and NOT function-local, so the names bind as `server` module attributes.\\n\\nCall sites inside `server.py` that must keep working with no edit: `_view_payload_token_count` (221), the match-context sizing call (648), the `_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET` check (1582).\\n\\nTest references that must keep working with no edit: `mocker.patch('backlog_core.server._enc.encode', ...)` (5 call sites in `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py`); `from backlog_core.server import _VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` / `_build_over_budget_view` / `_sections_index_from_result`; attribute access `server._token_count`, `server._VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET`, `server._filter_view_sections` in `backlog_core/tests/test_view_over_budget_gate.py` and `test_view_pagination_section_index.py`.\\n\\n## Step 4 \\u2014 conftest docstring correction (architect spec section 6.5)\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/conftest.py`'s module docstring states that importing `backlog_core.server` initializes `server._enc = tiktoken.get_encoding('cl100k_base')` at module load. After this move that claim is stale: `_enc` is initialized in `view_budget.py` and reaches `server._enc` via the re-export. The pre-warming BEHAVIOUR is unaffected (it seeds `tiktoken.registry.ENCODINGS` globally, not a module attribute), so no functional test change is needed \\u2014 but the docstring's factual claim about which module initializes it must be corrected. One-line edit, e.g. `view_budget._enc (re-exported as server._enc)`.\\n\\nThis is in scope for this phase, not a follow-up: leaving a docstring asserting an inaccurate fact about the codebase's own import structure is exactly the drift this refactor exists to eliminate (feature-context outcome #1).\",\"constraints\":\"- ZERO behavioural change in this phase.\\n- The `from .view_budget import (...)` block in `server.py` MUST be a plain module-level import so the names bind as `server` attributes. A `view_budget.<name>`-qualified internal reference style would break `mocker.patch` and is not acceptable.\\n- Do NOT implement the bottom-of-file placement workaround unless Step 1 forces a divergence.\\n- Plain module name `view_budget.py`.\\n- `from __future__ import annotations` first import; full return-type annotations.\\n- Do NOT touch `operations.py`.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/view_budget.py`; modified `server.py`; one-line docstring correction in `backlog_core/tests/conftest.py`.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/view_budget.py` exists containing the six symbols plus `_enc` (or fewer, with a recorded divergence per Step 1).\\n- Its module docstring describes `_token_count` as general token-counting infrastructure, not view-exclusive, and names the two non-view consumers.\\n- `_VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET` is annotated `Final[int]`.\\n- The `import-contract` check command exits 0.\\n- `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/ -q` and `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py -q` both pass with ZERO test-file modifications (the Step 4 conftest docstring edit is comment-only and does not count).\\n- `uv run pytest -q` passes.\\n- `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/*.py` passes.\\n- `server.py` line count is strictly lower than 4640.\\n- The MCP tool count is still 46.\\n- No `@mcp.tool()`-decorated function moved. Module name is `view_budget.py`, not `_view_budget.py`.\\n- `operations.py` is untouched (T2/T3 own it and run concurrently).\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run the `import-contract` check command \\u2014 must exit 0.\\n2. `uv run python -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'plugins/development-harness'); from backlog_core import server; print(server._enc, server._token_count, server._VIEW_TOKEN_BUDGET, server._filter_view_sections, server._sections_index_from_result)\\\"` \\u2014 every name must resolve as a `server` module attribute. This is the check that catches the silently-unpatched-mock failure mode.\\n3. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py -q` \\u2014 this is the file with the 5 `mocker.patch('backlog_core.server._enc.encode')` sites. It must pass unmodified.\\n4. Run the `mcp-tool-count` check command from the plan's acceptance-criteria-structured \\u2014 must print 46 and exit 0.\\n5. `uv run python plugins/development-harness/tests/characterise_view_path.py` and diff against the T0 record. Must be byte-identical: this phase changes no behaviour. (If T2 has already landed its dual-output fix in the same tree, diff against T2's post-fix record instead and expect the same single permitted difference, no more.)\\n6. `wc -l plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \\u2014 confirm reduction from 4640.\\n7. `git status --porcelain` \\u2014 confirm no test file is modified other than the conftest docstring line, and that `operations.py` is unmodified.\",\"handoff\":\"Report the importable-name list `view_budget.py` exposes, the post-T4 line count of `server.py`, and the observed MCP tool count. T5 verifies.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"high\"},{\"id\":\"T5\",\"title\":\"TN verification gate \\u2014 prove behavioural equivalence and adjudicate the one intended change\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"dh:tn-verification-gate\",\"dependencies\":[\"T1\",\"T2\",\"T3\",\"T4\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:p